# Typescript

Follow industry best practices, except where it would lead to complex code that is difficult for novices to read.

## Rules of thumb

Avoid the use of the `any` type, but it is acceptable when we want to avoid complex generics and abstractions that will clutter the codebase.

Make use of the `type-fest` library's utility types to write cleaner, simpler code.
